WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
A small bakery has six keen
people asking for a job.

2
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.680
Every one of them would work hard.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.090
Every one would make more bread.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.670
Yet the owner hires only four.

5
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.390
Nobody buys workers for their own sake.

6
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.120
So what decides how many
a business wants to hire?

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.160
In this mission, you'll see why
the demand for workers slopes down,

8
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.060
and what makes it shift.

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.780
Then you'll learn to tell
a movement along the curve

10
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.170
from a shift of the whole curve.

11
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.490
Your mission: find out what
really decides the number

12
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.270
of workers a firm takes on.
